---
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro'
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
import { recordExample } from '../../lib/api-reference.js'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Getting started"
  description="Set up native CEF browser capture, recording and rendering."
  section="overview"
>
  <h1>Native browser recording</h1>
  <h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
  <p>
    Use Node.js 22+, FFmpeg/FFprobe and a separately built native CEF browser. macOS ARM64 has
    historical native verification. Linux remains unverified; Windows packaging is not implemented.
  </p>
  <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
  <p>
    Follow the <a href="https://github.com/skyaara/suitecut/blob/main/native/browser/README.md"
      >native build instructions</a
    > and set the browser executable path.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    label="Terminal"
    code={'pnpm install --frozen-lockfile\npnpm build\nexport SUITECUT_NATIVE_EXECUTABLE="/absolute/path/to/suitecut-browser"\nnode dist/cli.js doctor'}
  />
  <h2 id="record-a-flow">Record a flow</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={recordExample} />
  <h2 id="run-and-render">Run and render</h2>
  <p>
    The recorder closes its primary browser, saves source clips and writes a manifest. The renderer
    composes selected intervals and mixes page audio with narration.
  </p>
  <h2 id="render-quality">Render quality</h2>
  <p>
    Choose output dimensions, FPS 1–120, quality profiles and supported FFmpeg encoders. Higher
    output FPS can repeat captured images; it does not create motion the browser did not capture.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
